  "title": "Where a dissonance sits among atoms",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "At genus 2 a state at the floor W = 1 is one over-agreeing face with no violated line or even face, so learning with the state fixed cannot move it (proved). Computed on K_2 and K_3 with one or two Fano atoms: the dissonance moves down into an atom by growth at the dissonance, and the sight-4 learner then resolves it there or leaves one unit inside the other atom, present since that atom was grown; with atoms away from the dissonance the sight-4 learner is stuck; the floor unit can sit inside atoms on every space and at the upper level on half.",
